# Checkov project basics

- Say **check** or **policy**, not "control". Shipped IDs are `CKV_<PROVIDER>_<N>` (Python) or `CKV2_<PROVIDER>_<N>` (YAML graph).
- Python Terraform checks live in `checkov/terraform/checks/resource/<provider>/` (also `data/` / `provider/`). YAML graph checks live in `checkov/terraform/checks/graph_checks/<provider>/`.
- GRC requests use the **GRC new check request** GitHub issue form. Engineers implement them with the `add-terraform-check` skill (`gh issue view`, comment mapping questions on the issue, then scaffold check + tests). Record IaC assumptions on the PR.
- New checks need pass **and** fail fixtures parsed through the **runner**. Assert **which resource IDs** pass/fail, not only counts. Do not hand-build conf dicts.
- PR titles drive the changelog: `feat(terraform): add CKV_GCP_128 to ensure …`. Allowed scopes are listed in `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`.
- Do not fill retired ID gaps. Allocate **max existing number + 1** for that prefix. `test_no_missing_ids` enforces sequences (GCP Python skips `CKV_GCP_5`, `_19`, `_67`).
